        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): stop ignored disabled servers from starting",
        "body": "Closes #103954\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators could set `disabled: true` on an MCP server, see the config accepted without warning, and still have OpenClaw start that server process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOpenClaw now reports the ineffective `disabled` key with actionable `enabled: false` guidance. `openclaw doctor --fix` migrates boolean `disabled` values to the inverse canonical `enabled` value, preserving an explicitly configured canonical value when both fields exist. The repair follows supported single-file `$include` ownership and continues to fail closed for root, array, nested, or sibling-override include layouts. Runtime consumers remain on the single `enabled` contract; no compatibility alias was added to steady-state startup code.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators with the reported config get a clear validation error instead of a silently ignored setting. Running `openclaw doctor --fix` repairs existing root files and supported single-file includes, after which disabled MCP servers are excluded from runtime startup.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal on-disk include proof used an `openclaw.json5` root containing `mcp: { $include: \"./mcp.json5\" }`. The included file defined a disabled stdio server whose command would create a marker file if launched. The proof ran the production snapshot resolver, doctor migration, include-aware config writer, and session MCP runtime catalog (the process-launch boundary):\n\n```text\n{\"doctorWrite\":\"single-file include preserved\",\"migrated\":{\"enabled\":false,\"command\":\"/bin/sh\",\"args\":[\"-c\",\"touch /private/tmp/openclaw-103970-proof/mcp-started; sleep 30\"]},\"runtimeServers\":[],\"processMarker\":\"absent\"}\n```\n\nPost-proof filesystem assertions:\n\n```text\nroot openclaw.json5: still contains only mcp.$include; no disabledProof server was flattened into root\nincluded mcp.json5: contains \"enabled\": false; no \"disabled\" key remains\nruntime catalog: zero configured MCP servers\nprocess marker: absent\n```\n\nFocused and caller validation on the final committed diff:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/config/mutate.test.ts \\\n  src/config/schema.test.ts \\\n  src/commands/doctor/shared/config-flow-steps.test.ts \\\n  src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrate.test.ts \\\n  src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/update-cli.test.ts -- --reporter=dot\n\n5 routed Vitest shards passed:\n- config mutation: 128 tests\n- doctor health persistence: 91 tests\n- schema + legacy migration: 99 tests\n- update CLI: 181 tests\n- doctor config flow: 11 tests\n- total: 510 tests\n\nnode scripts/run-oxlint.mjs <seven touched TypeScript files>\n0 errors\n\noxfmt <eight touched files>\nclean\n\ngit diff --check\nclean\n```\n\nFresh autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings. Blacksmith Testbox could not be allocated because the `blacksmith` CLI is unavailable on this host; the narrow bundled-Node fallback and direct on-disk production-boundary proof above were used instead.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed and understand the schema, migration precedence, include write ownership, runtime exclusion path, and tests in this change.\n",
